<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST807"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Superbike7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Superbike7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 17, 2004 - 7:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jacob Allen was tied to a railroad track with bailing wire and was struck by a train July 5 2004 at about 3 am near Milan Kansas. The rumor is that BTKs last letter at the library claimed with evidence that he was responsible for this crime. It seemed to fit to me because of cruelty of this crime, so I thought could this have been a crime that has occurred already or even been written in a true crime as a fiction story that BTK fantasized about and then commited. I was floored when I found that a book had been written about a crime In Mena Ark. where two teens had been killed by being placed on a railroad tracks by drug related criminals as revenge for informing on them.I think BTK fantisizes about his crimes and then is highly organized in his detail in the commitment of his crimes. He is also attracted to crimes with alot of flair or unusual cruelty. Jacob Allen was a young man an athelete, what cunning it would take to get him controled by a man who is at least 50. What a challenge, Gacy was very good at doing this by using drugs alcohol and handcuffs or sex as bait. I picture BTK living in rural area south of Wichita like the tooth fairy in red dragaon in an area where no one is too close. Most of his murders were south or east of wichata there are also a rash of unsolved murders southwest of Wichita. One more note this area overlaps several different juristrictions of police which I beleive could only help you get away with murder <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 807-->
<!--Post: 808--><!--Time: 1092797390-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST808"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 17, 2004 - 7:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rumors about Jacob&#39;s death span from BTK to suicide. It was horrible what happened to him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 808-->
<!--Post: 812--><!--Time: 1092799382-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST812"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 17, 2004 - 8:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting that it occurred on July 5th.  Z shot Darlene Ferrin and Mike Mageau around midnight, either just prior on July 4th or just after on July 5th; Darlene was DOA at the hospital at 12:38 AM 7-5-1969. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 812-->
<!--Post: 815--><!--Time: 1092807158-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST815"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 17, 2004 - 10:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If this is BTK, it&#39;s interesting that he killed a man. Latet homosexual? Otero and Bright had significant latent homosexual aspects, especially Otero. <BR> <BR>Please don&#39;t take this the wrong way but Shirley Vian was a little, well, mannish, too. And is another indication of latent homosexuality. <BR> <BR>As to BTK in his 50s &#40;I agree, Superbike7, with that age estimate&#41; and a much younger who was quite athletic and would presumably be able to fend off an attacker. &#40;Unless the attacker had a firearm and knew to stand about six or eight feet from the victims, so as not to lose control of the gun.&#41; Anyway, the age difference. &#40;Begin Douglas-O-of-Ted fame parody&#41;: <BR> <BR>We musn&#39;t overlook the element of surprise. We musn&#39;t jump to conclusions; just because it looks like a sperm overshooting an ovary does not mean it is either sperm or ovary. Ted wrote manically but brilliantly, yet reseved his most stultifying prose for public occasions. We musn&#39;t be fooled by appearances.&#34; <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 815-->
<!--Post: 819--><!--Time: 1092932121-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST819"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 19, 2004 - 9:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Don&#39;t overlook stun gun usage. It might be impossible to detect stungun markings on a body destroyed by a train. Current stun guns run as high as 625,000&#43; volts. It is also possible to buy veterinary drugs in ag supply stores, including tranquilizing drugs, some which have a paralytic effect. Those may or may not show on a tox screen, depending on what substances are being searched. If, with blinders on, they searched for cocaine, THC, meth, Xanax, etc., it is possible to overlook some others. One of the first &#34;Unsolved Mystery&#34; Cases was just that. It took 3 exhumations before they identified the veterinary substance that produced paralysis but kept the victim perfectly conscious. <BR> <BR>With such a fresh, local kill, BTK may do cemetery visiting as well. Surely he watches the Cold Cases on A&amp;E, etc. We may soon, if we haven&#39;t already, see him copycat some of those.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 819-->
<!--Post: 1115--><!--Time: 1097190892-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1115"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 07, 2004 - 4:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read today that his death was ruled a suicide. He staged it to look like a homicide. I find that strange indeed unless there was insurance monies involved that would not pay in case of a suicide. Or perhaps he tried to save face for his family.  <BR> <BR>I live in the county where the &#39;Passion of the Christ&#39; murder confession took place. That was initially ruled a suicide as well. We can only wait and see.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1115-->
<!--Post: 1444--><!--Time: 1101319150-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1444"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, November 24, 2004 - 9:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is an article on the net saying that the local citizenry of Argonia do not buy the suicide ruling. An article in which the train crew were interviewed stated that he was naked. Of course, his clothing could have been stipped off as a result of the impact. That is not unusual in hit and run incidents. <BR> <BR>Perhaps the police are trying subterfuge and disinformation to avert panic and increase overconfidence in a possible killer. This also reduces vigilance on the part of others as they think that they have no reason to be guarded and watchful. Sad anyway you look at it.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1444-->
